From e8a5a685d1572cc76885f6348d778aa70ec8df5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:51:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(kms-worker): Profile Q in the connector (lifecycle
 Level 3)

The PQ-only operator policy of the Decryption Authority Lifecycle draft,
setting `profile_q` (off by default), module core/profile_q.rs:

- Q1: one canonical statement (chain, ACL, variant, B_Q, the ICS's
  keccak256), signed by each operator with ML-DSA-65. At startup the worker
  counts distinct operators whose signature verifies under its K8 mode and
  establishes the profile only with at least `threshold` (n - t) and only for
  a statement naming its chain, ACL and ICS. No setting and no on-chain read
  can engage it. Requires Profile H.
- Q4: Profile H's signature check gets the profile for the chain (the shared
  crate decides by the signer's code at the pinned block); once engaged, the
  legacy gateway path, whose signature is checked by ECDSA only, is refused.
- Q5: after the delegated view answers true, a delegation from a delegator
  with no code, an EIP-7702 or an EIP-7851 indicator counts only if its
  per-contract or wildcard record is active and unchanged since B_Q. The
  records are read with eth_getStorageAt from Zama's ERC-7201 ACLStorage, at
  one pinned block, for ACL versions whose layout is known; others fail
  closed. Refusals are final (acl_denied).

Errors: ProfileQRefused maps to a final user_signature_rejected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
